bunch of ideas wrapped together :-) :-(

I've been re-thinking the bard class... the essence of the idea still
makes sense to me, but the whole implementation still seems too much.
Maybe a bard can be implemented in nethack in a simpler way, without
so much hassle.

So, how about a bard class who simply can use any common musical
instrument as a magic one? Someone else thinks this can lead to a
different gameplay syle?
I'm thinking of pulling off of the patch all the parts that implement
the concept of music skill and just making the bard play normal
instruments as if it were magical, wasting some of his MP.
Additionaly, he could get to skilled in enchantment spells.

The bard would then start the game with a wooden flute, which he can
use to make monsters sleep; I think it's better not giving him a
starting wooden harp because it seems to me having a way to tame
monsters right from the start of the game is too unbalancing.
Additionaly, he can use:
- tin whistles as magic ones;
- leather drums as drums of earthquake;
- tooled horns as fire or frost ones;
- and the quest artifact could then play all the effects above, at the
player choice.

I'm also thinking about giving an effect to bugles, perhaps scare
monster. And also thinking of mantaining satyrs and syrinxes (reed
flutes) because it gives bards a good chance of having another
instrument, besides the starting one, since it is difficult to find a
random-generated one. I'm not sure about what magical effect reed
flutes can have, though.

